---
import ArticleClosingNote from '@/components/articles/ArticleClosingNote.astro';
import ArticleImage from '@/components/ui/ArticleImage.astro';

import oldTownStreetScene from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-old-town-street-scene.webp";
import oldTownKnight from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-old-town-medieval-knight.webp";
import koukosRestaurant from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-koukos-restaurant.webp";
import koukosBreakfast from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-koukos-breakfast.webp";
import dreamCream from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-dream-cream.webp";
import symiHarbour from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/symi-island-colourful-harbour.webp";
import symiShopfront from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/symi-town-colourful-shopfront.webp";
import symiStreetCafes from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/symi-town-street-cafes.webp";
import symiArchitecture from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/symi-traditional-architecture.webp";
import symiYialaBeach from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/symi-yiala-beach.webp";
import symiYialaBeach2 from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/greece-symi-yiala-beach.webp";
import lindosTraditionalStreet from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-lindos-village-traditional-street.webp";
import lindosWhitewashedStreet from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-lindos-village-whitewashed-street.webp";
import lindosExploring from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-exploring-lindos-village.webp";
import stPaulsBay from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-lindos-st-paul's-bay.webp";
import stPaulsBayBeach from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-lindos-st-paul's-beach.webp";
import lindosSunriseViewpoint from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-lindos-sunrise-viewpoint.webp";
import lindosAcropolis from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-lindos-akropolis.webp";
import kallitheaEntrance from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-kallithea-springs-entrance.webp";
import kallitheaSprings from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-kallithea-springs.webp";
import kallitheaBeachView from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-kallithea-springs-beach-view.webp";
import anthonyQuinnBay from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-anthony-quinn-bay.webp";
import kounnaRestoBar from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-kounna-beach-resto-bar.webp";
import kounnaCoffeeView from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-kounna-beach-coffee-with-view.webp";
import myrovolosRestaurant from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-myrovolos-restaurant.webp";
import myrovolosMezedopoleion from "@/assets/articles/rhodes/rhodes-myrovolos-restaurant-mezedopoleion.webp";

const prose = 'article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0';
const twoColGrid = 'grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4';
const symiGrid = 'my-5 grid grid-cols-1 items-start gap-3 sm:grid-cols-5 md:my-8 md:gap-4';
const kallitheaGrid = 'my-5 grid grid-cols-1 items-start gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3 md:my-8 md:gap-4';
---

<section id="section-0" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Day 1: Rhodes Old Town &amp; Mandraki Harbour</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <h4 class="mb-3 text-black">Explore Rhodes Old Town</h4>
    <p>Rhodes Old Town is one of the best-preserved medieval towns in Europe and a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Surrounded by impressive stone walls, it's home to historic streets, medieval gates, local shops and landmarks like the Palace of the Grand Master and the Street of the Knights.</p>
    <div class="max-w-md">
      <ArticleImage src={oldTownStreetScene} alt="Street scene in the medieval streets of Rhodes Old Town" caption="Wandering the medieval streets" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>
    <p>I started my walk at Saint John's Gate, one of the main entrances to the Old Town, before slowly making my way through its narrow streets. Leave some time to wander through the quieter streets and see where they lead, and make sure not to miss the Street of the Knights, one of the most famous streets in Rhodes, as well as the Palace of the Grand Master, one of the town's most impressive landmarks.</p>
    <div class="max-w-md">
      <ArticleImage src={oldTownKnight} alt="A person dressed as a medieval knight in Rhodes Old Town" caption="A medieval knight near the Palace of the Grand Master" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>
    <p>Near the Palace of the Grand Master, I even came across someone dressed as a medieval knight, which added an extra touch to the whole experience and made the city's history feel even more alive.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Lunch at Koukos</h4>
    <p>Housed in a beautifully restored traditional building, Koukos is home to a boutique hotel, bakery, café and restaurant, making it an ideal stop for lunch after exploring Rhodes Old Town.</p>
    <p>I ended up eating here more than once during my trip, stopping by for both breakfast and lunch on different days. Everything I ordered was excellent, which is why it's one of the places I'd happily return to on my next visit to Rhodes.</p>
    <div class={twoColGrid}>
      <ArticleImage src={koukosRestaurant} alt="Koukos restaurant in Rhodes" caption="Koukos" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
      <ArticleImage src={koukosBreakfast} alt="Breakfast served at Koukos in Rhodes" caption="A relaxed lunch stop" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Optional: Dream Cream</h4>
    <p>If you're in the mood for something sweet after lunch, Dream Cream is just a short walk from Koukos. Whether you fancy gelato, waffles or pancakes, it's a great place to treat yourself before continuing your walk towards Mandraki Harbour.</p>
    <div class="max-w-md">
      <ArticleImage src={dreamCream} alt="Sweet treats from Dream Cream in Rhodes" caption="A sweet stop at Dream Cream" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Walk to Mandraki Harbour</h4>
    <p>Mandraki Harbour is one of Rhodes' most recognisable landmarks, known for its historic windmills, colourful boats and waterfront promenade. It's the perfect place for a walk after exploring the Old Town and offers a completely different side of the island.</p>
    <p>I loved walking along the harbour in the late afternoon, when the temperature was a little cooler and the waterfront felt much livelier. After spending the morning surrounded by medieval streets and stone walls, it was a nice change of scenery before dinner.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Dinner at Taverna Kostas</h4>
    <p>Taverna Kostas was another recommendation from local friends in Rhodes, and it quickly became one of my favourite meals on the island. Tucked away in a quiet street of the Old Town, this family-run taverna serves traditional Greek dishes in a warm and welcoming atmosphere, making it the perfect place to end your first day.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-1" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Day 2: Symi Island Day Trip</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <h4 class="mb-3 text-black">Take the Ferry to Symi</h4>
    <p>If you're spending five days in Rhodes, don't miss the opportunity to visit Symi. When planning my trip, I had to decide between Symi and Halki, as both islands are frequently recommended by locals as day trips from Rhodes. In the end, I chose Symi—and as soon as the ferry started approaching the harbour, I knew I had made the right choice.</p>
    <p>The moment the ferry begins approaching the harbour, it's almost impossible to stop taking photos. The colourful houses climbing up the hillside create one of the most beautiful arrivals I've experienced on a Greek island, and honestly, I don't think photos fully capture how impressive it looks in person.</p>
    <p>I originally looked at one of the smaller excursion boats, but they were already fully booked. Instead, I travelled on the regular ferry, which turned out to be a great choice.</p>
    <ArticleImage src={symiHarbour} alt="The colourful harbour of Symi island with houses climbing the hillside" caption="Arriving into Symi's colourful harbour" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Wander Through the Streets of Symi</h4>
    <p>Before heading anywhere specific, spend some time exploring the harbour area and wandering through the small streets. If you don't mind a few steps, walk up part of the historic Kali Strata for some of the best views over the harbour.</p>
    <p>What stood out to me most was how photogenic the entire island felt. Around almost every corner, you'll find colourful houses, traditional architecture and beautiful sea views that make you want to stop and take another photo. It's the kind of place that's best explored without a plan.</p>
    <div class={symiGrid}>
      <div class="sm:col-span-3">
        <ArticleImage src={symiArchitecture} alt="Traditional architecture in Symi Town" caption="Traditional Symi architecture" figureClass="m-0" />
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 sm:col-span-2 md:gap-4">
        <ArticleImage src={symiShopfront} alt="A colourful shopfront in Symi Town" caption="Colourful shopfronts around every corner in Symi" figureClass="m-0" />
        <ArticleImage src={symiStreetCafes} alt="Street cafes in Symi Town" caption="Cafes lining the streets of Symi" figureClass="m-0" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Stop by The Panormitis Bakery (Gialos Branch)</h4>
    <p>If you're looking for a quick snack while exploring Symi, I'd recommend stopping by The Panormitis Bakery (Gialos Branch). It's a popular local bakery serving traditional pies and freshly baked treats, and if you're anything like me, you'll probably struggle to leave with just one thing.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Relax by the Sea</h4>
    <p>After exploring Symi Town, spend the rest of the afternoon by the sea. I walked to Yiala Beach, about 30 minutes from the harbour, and it turned out to be one of my favourite parts of the day. The water was crystal clear, there were very few people around, and it was the perfect place to relax before returning to Rhodes.</p>
    <div class={twoColGrid}>
      <ArticleImage src={symiYialaBeach} alt="The clear water at Yiala Beach in Symi" caption="Yiala Beach — clear water and a quiet afternoon" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
      <ArticleImage src={symiYialaBeach2} alt="The coastline at Yiala Beach in Symi" caption="Plenty of quiet swimming spots along the coast" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>
    <p>If Yiala Beach feels a little too far, don't worry about reaching a specific beach. Symi has plenty of beautiful swimming spots along the coastline, so it's easy to stop wherever catches your eye and enjoy a swim.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Return to Rhodes</h4>
    <p>As the ferry heads back to Rhodes, you'll get one last view of Symi's colourful harbour. It was easily one of the highlights of my trip, and a day I'd happily repeat on my next visit.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-2" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Day 3: Discover Lindos Village &amp; St. Paul's Bay</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <h4 class="mb-3 text-black">Explore Lindos Village</h4>
    <p>I would highly recommend spending at least one night in Lindos rather than visiting on a day trip. This small village is one hour drive from Rhodes town and one of the most picturesque places in Greece. With its whitewashed houses, narrow streets and hilltop Acropolis overlooking the sea, it's easy to see why it's one of Rhodes' most iconic places to visit.</p>
    <p>Out of everywhere I visited in Rhodes, this was the place that felt most like a traditional Greek island.</p>
    <p><a href="https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Lindos%2C+Rhodes%2C+Greece" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">🏨 Compare hotels in Lindos</a></p>
    <div class={twoColGrid}>
      <ArticleImage src={lindosTraditionalStreet} alt="A traditional street in Lindos Village" caption="Traditional streets of Lindos" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
      <ArticleImage src={lindosWhitewashedStreet} alt="A whitewashed street in Lindos Village" caption="Whitewashed alleyways and hidden corners" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>
    <ArticleImage src={lindosExploring} alt="Exploring the narrow streets of Lindos Village" caption="Wandering through Lindos once the day visitors leave" />

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Visit St. Paul's Bay</h4>
    <p>A short walk from the village brings you to St. Paul's Bay, one of the most beautiful beaches in Rhodes.</p>
    <p>The combination of crystal-clear water, dramatic cliffs and views of the Acropolis creates one of the most photogenic spots on the island. Whether you decide to swim or simply enjoy the view, it's easy to spend much longer here than you originally planned.</p>
    <div class={twoColGrid}>
      <ArticleImage src={stPaulsBay} alt="St. Paul's Bay in Lindos with views towards the Acropolis" caption="St. Paul's Bay" />
      <ArticleImage src={stPaulsBayBeach} alt="The beach at St. Paul's Bay in Lindos" caption="Crystal-clear water at St. Paul's Bay" />
    </div>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Lunch at Tambakio</h4>
    <p>Set right on the edge of St. Paul's Bay, Tambakio offers front-row views of the crystal-clear water in one of the most beautiful settings in Lindos. Even if you're only stopping for a drink, the location alone makes it worth the visit.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Dinner at Acropolis Roof Garden Restaurant</h4>
    <p>As the sun begins to set over Lindos, head to Acropolis Roof Garden Restaurant for dinner. Perched above the village, it offers beautiful views of both the Acropolis and the sea, making it one of the best places to enjoy the evening. If you can, book a table in advance for one of the outdoor tables.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-3" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Day 4: Sunrise, Acropolis &amp; Return to Rhodes Town</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <h4 class="mb-3 text-black">Watch Sunrise Over Lindos</h4>
    <p>If you're happy to wake up early, sunrise is one of the best times to experience Lindos. I watched the sunrise from Lindos Viewpoint, and it's a spot I'd happily recommend to anyone visiting the village. From here, you'll have panoramic views over the Acropolis, St. Paul's Bay and the whitewashed houses of Lindos as the sun begins to rise.</p>
    <ArticleImage src={lindosSunriseViewpoint} alt="Sunrise viewpoint overlooking Lindos" caption="Sunrise over Lindos" imgClass="aspect-[5/4] object-cover" />

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Breakfast at Melia</h4>
    <p>After sunrise, head to Melia for breakfast. Its rooftop garden offers lovely views towards Lindos and the Acropolis, making it the perfect place to relax before continuing your day.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Visit the Acropolis of Lindos</h4>
    <p>After breakfast, make your way up to the Acropolis before the temperatures begin to rise.</p>
    <ArticleImage src={lindosAcropolis} alt="The Acropolis of Lindos overlooking the village and coastline" caption="The Acropolis of Lindos" imgClass="aspect-[5/4] object-cover" />
    <p>This is one of the most important archaeological sites in Rhodes, and visiting early makes the experience much more enjoyable during the summer months. The views from the top over Lindos, St. Paul's Bay, and the coastline are easily among the best on the island.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Lunch at Mythos</h4>
    <p>Before leaving Lindos, stop by Mythos All Day Restaurant for lunch. Its rooftop terrace overlooks both the Acropolis and the harbour, making it the perfect place for one last meal before heading back to Rhodes Town.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-4" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Day 5: Kallithea Springs &amp; Anthony Quinn Bay</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <h4 class="mb-3 text-black">Visit Kallithea Springs</h4>
    <p>Spend your final day in Rhodes exploring two of the island's most beautiful coastal spots, starting with Kallithea Springs.</p>
    <div class={kallitheaGrid}>
      <div class="sm:col-span-2">
        <ArticleImage src={kallitheaEntrance} alt="The entrance to Kallithea Springs in Rhodes" caption="Kallithea Springs" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" figureClass="m-0" />
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 sm:col-span-1 md:gap-4">
        <ArticleImage src={kallitheaSprings} alt="The Italian-inspired architecture of Kallithea Springs" caption="Italian-inspired architecture" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" figureClass="m-0" />
        <ArticleImage src={kallitheaBeachView} alt="The seaside setting and clear water at Kallithea Springs" caption="Crystal-clear waters" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" figureClass="m-0" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>Originally known for its thermal baths, today it's best known for its beautiful architecture, seaside setting and crystal-clear waters. The combination of Italian-inspired buildings, stone pathways and coastal views makes it one of the most photogenic places in Rhodes.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Spend the Afternoon at Anthony Quinn Bay</h4>
    <p>From Kallithea Springs, continue to Anthony Quinn Bay, one of the most famous beaches in Rhodes.</p>
    <ArticleImage src={anthonyQuinnBay} alt="The turquoise water and rocky surroundings of Anthony Quinn Bay in Rhodes" caption="Anthony Quinn Bay" imgClass="aspect-[5/4] object-cover" />
    <p>Known for its turquoise waters and dramatic rocky surroundings, it's easy to see why this bay has become one of the island's most photographed spots. Seeing it from above gave me a completely different appreciation for its colours and shape. I would recommend arriving earlier in the day, as the beach tends to get busier later on.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Lunch at Kounna</h4>
    <p>If you're looking for somewhere to stop for lunch or a drink, Kounna is a great choice. Perched above Anthony Quinn Bay, it offers beautiful views over the bay and is the perfect place to take a break after a swim. Even if you're only stopping for a coffee, the view alone makes it worth the visit.</p>
    <div class={twoColGrid}>
      <ArticleImage src={kounnaRestoBar} alt="Kounna beach resto-bar above Anthony Quinn Bay" caption="Kounna" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
      <ArticleImage src={kounnaCoffeeView} alt="Coffee with a coastline view at Kounna" caption="Coffee with a view over the coastline" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Dinner at Myrovolos</h4>
    <p>Myrovolos is a modern meze restaurant serving traditional Greek dishes with a contemporary twist. If you're looking for somewhere special for your final dinner in Rhodes, this is a great choice.</p>
    <div class={twoColGrid}>
      <ArticleImage src={myrovolosRestaurant} alt="Myrovolos restaurant in Rhodes" caption="Myrovolos" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
      <ArticleImage src={myrovolosMezedopoleion} alt="Meze dishes at Myrovolos mezedopoleion in Rhodes" caption="A modern meze spread" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>
    <p>It was recommended to me by local friends from Rhodes, so I knew it had to be good. My husband and I ordered several small dishes to share, and honestly, I couldn't tell you which one was my favourite. Every single dish was excellent, making it one of the best meals we had during our trip.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-5" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Where to Stay in Rhodes</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>I'd recommend using Rhodes Town as your base for this itinerary. From there, you can easily visit Symi, Kallithea Springs, Anthony Quinn Bay and other nearby attractions without having to change hotels. The only exception is Lindos, where I'd recommend spending one night to experience the village after the day visitors leave.</p>
    <h4 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-black">Luxury</h4>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 marker:text-black/40">
      <li class="prose-body"><a href="https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Rodos+Park+Suites+%26+Spa+Rhodes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">Rodos Park, an SLH Hotel</a> – Luxury spa hotel with elegant gardens.</li>
      <li class="prose-body"><a href="https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Allegory+Boutique+Hotel+Rhodes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">Allegory Boutique Hotel</a> – Boutique hotel in a restored medieval building.</li>
    </ul>
    <h4 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-black">Mid-range</h4>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 marker:text-black/40">
      <li class="prose-body"><a href="https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Old+Town+Senses+Boutique+Hotel+Rhodes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">Old Town Senses Boutique Hotel</a> – Stylish boutique hotel with modern design.</li>
      <li class="prose-body"><a href="https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Canvas+by+Mitsis+Petit+Palais+Rhodes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">Canvas by Mitsis Petit Palais</a> – Modern hotel with excellent breakfast.</li>
    </ul>
    <h4 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-black">Budget</h4>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 marker:text-black/40">
      <li class="prose-body"><a href="https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Saint+Michel+Rhodes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">Saint Michel</a> – Family-run guesthouse with authentic character.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-6" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>FAQ</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={`${prose} space-y-6`}>
    <div id="faq-0" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">1. How do you get to Rhodes?</h4>
      <p>The easiest way to reach Rhodes is by flying into Rhodes International Airport (Diagoras), which has direct flights from many European cities during the summer, as well as regular domestic flights from Athens and Thessaloniki.</p>
      <p>If you're already travelling around Greece, you can also reach Rhodes by ferry from Athens (Piraeus) and several nearby islands, although ferry journeys are considerably longer than flying.</p>
      <p><a href="https://www.skyscanner.net/flights-to/rho/cheap-flights-to-rhodes-airport.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">✈️ Compare flights to Rhodes</a></p>
      <p><a href="https://www.directferries.com/rhodes_ferry.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">⛴️ Compare ferry tickets to Rhodes</a></p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-1" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">2. How do you get around Rhodes?</h4>
      <p>Renting a car is the best way to explore Rhodes. It gives you the flexibility to visit places like Lindos, Kallithea Springs and Anthony Quinn Bay at your own pace, without relying on public transport or organised tours.</p>
      <p><a href="https://www.discovercars.com/greece/rhodes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">🚗 Compare car rental prices in Rhodes</a></p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-2" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">3. What is the best time to visit Rhodes?</h4>
      <p>If I were planning another trip to Rhodes, I'd choose May, June, September or October. The weather is warm enough to enjoy the beaches, but much more comfortable for sightseeing than during the peak summer months.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-3" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">4. How do you get to Lindos?</h4>
      <p>Lindos is about a one-hour drive from Rhodes Town. Since the village is pedestrian-only, you'll need to leave your car in one of the parking areas just outside the village and continue on foot. From there, everything is within easy walking distance.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-4" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">5. How do you get to Symi Island?</h4>
      <p>The easiest way to get to Symi is by taking the regular ferry from Rhodes. The journey usually takes around one hour, depending on the ferry you choose, making it an easy and comfortable day trip. I'd recommend booking both your outbound and return tickets at the same time, especially during the summer months.</p>
      <p><a href="https://www.directferries.com/symi_ferry.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">⛴️ Compare ferry tickets to Symi</a></p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-5" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">6. Do you need a car in Symi?</h4>
      <p>Not for a day trip. I explored Symi entirely on foot and never felt like I needed a car. Most visitors spend their time around Symi Town, where everything is within walking distance.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-7" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class={prose}>
    <ArticleClosingNote label="Final thoughts">
      <p>In just a few days, I found myself wandering through medieval streets, exploring the colourful harbour of Symi, watching the sunrise over Lindos and swimming in some of the clearest water I've seen in Greece.</p>
      <p>If you're planning your first trip to Rhodes, I hope this itinerary helps you make the most of your time on the island—and I hope Rhodes becomes one of your favourite places in Greece too.</p>
